  "configuration_id": "config_021",
  "reason": "The current best is config_033 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, multiprofile) at 0.725 acc / 0.685 F1 with only 3.60 GPU hours. All completed experiments use multiprofile, so a key uncertainty remains: does multiprofile aggregation actually add value over a single profile when paired with the strongest encoders? config_021 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, singleprofile, weighted) directly tests this with the best-known encoder pair. If singleprofile matches or approaches 0.725, it confirms a much cheaper architecture (no aggregation step, ~2–3 GPU hours) and frees remaining budget for fine-tuning. If it falls well short, it confirms that multiprofile + transformer aggregation is essential, and the remaining 3 experiments can focus on exploiting the multiprofile direction (e.g., testing pca_n2000 as a cheaper RNA encoder with imagenet_vit_l, or exploring scgpt+vit). This is the highest-information experiment: it resolves a fundamental architectural question while using the proven best encoders, at an expected cost of roughly 2–3 GPU hours (cheaper than the multiprofile transformer configs due to no aggregation module)."
}

